  "title": "S4 counting is #P-hard on closed manifolds with first homology Z/2",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from closed 3-manifold groups with bounded first homology into S4",
  "conclusion": "For every knot, the S4 counts of 2- and 4-surgery satisfy C2 + C4 = 8 + 3T, and 3 C2(K) + C2(K # trefoil) = 16 + 12T, where T counts transposition colourings. With the independently replayed knot hardness, counting homomorphisms to S4 is #P-hard on closed 3-manifolds with first homology Z/2, where metabelian targets stay polynomial.",
